						<td width="100%" class="body" valign="top">
														Well Seraphnie and I have decided to leave DragonsFist.<br />
<br />
Why.<br />
<br />
Well this incident does not add up for one.<br />
Salorn Claims that he had stopped people from accessing his account 3 weeks ago, he was dismissed appx 1 week ago after confronting Baker whom was tgressus.<br />
<br />
Salorn was inquiring to tgressus about Fullmetal who stated that Baker account was stolen. It is said that the account was bought fairly. Whatever the case may be on that, it resulted in other people disliking Dragons Fist, as those whom used the account before are upset about the matter.<br />
<br />
Openly attacking an officer started with Tg playing the Baker account. A rude comment was made to Salorn in open guildchat that he was one step away from demotion and other crunchy comments. I am a master of spin control and know when I see it.<br />
<br />
I'm shocked from the effect that tgressus did this from the Baker account, all the while baker was a hidden officer of DF, I was not in the know that Baker was a bought account by our very officers or that our Officers were buying accounts at all to pump up the guild.<br />
<br />
The real Salorn, I believe was not &quot;Inappropriate&quot; with advances, however someone else playing account may have been. Which if that was the case and it was so bad at the time; why would'nt it be not be taken to a GM with reports at that time? Why wait to boot him until questioned about the bought account? <br />
<br />
All this cunundra just add's to the spice. <br />
<br />
This from Seraphnie and I.  We personally do not believe that as player's of Everquest for 2 years now and being a couple that both work very hard on our characters that it's appropriate to buy accounts.<br />
<br />
The fundamental idea is horrid that we can not find guildies that have brought up and raised character's through hard work vs. Bought and payed for characters with a credit card and transfer. To me this is disgusting and inappropriate.<br />
<br />
It pretty much sucks the fun right outa the game.<br />
This is why we are leaving.<br />
<br />
The Accounts bought at officer level was never discussed with other officers as far as I know. I personally think that it should have been discussed amoung the officers and voted on whether or not buying accounts was ethical for our guild and ethical overall as players.<br />
<br />
But of course we know now. It is none of our business.<br />
<br />
Bickelhaupt, Aphrodyte and Hindo all good clerics in this guild for example, they now more or less being replaced with baker and other's on this bought account. This demotes their value to the guild and other clerics in our guild who work hard on their characters. This also drops the number of cool personalities we would strive for in our guild as the demand for say another class would be more or less balanced out with a bought account.<br />
<br />
Over all the effort to find good players reduces as accounts are bought and played.<br />
<br />
We have done our part about being honest and this last event goes beyond just dismissing an officer it goes with our honest belief that bought accounts are artifical ingredients and filler that take from the quality of the game and certainly take quality from a guild's demand for more great people.<br />
<br />
So not with a bang, not with a boom but a click on a nice afternoon...						</td>
